 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Hi. My name is Evan Kormos.",
   "start": 18.1,
   "end": 26.5
  },
  {
   "text": "I've been. Delivering, designing, building software for 20 years.",
   "start": 23.8,
   "end": 33.05
  },
  {
   "text": "The last 15 in enterprise financial services.",
   "start": 26.5,
   "end": 33.05
  },
  {
   "text": "I am a player coach at Coinbase.",
   "start": 33.05,
   "end": 37.3
  },
  {
   "text": "And we're here today to talk about trusting agents and policy-driven workflows.",
   "start": 37.3,
   "end": 42.85
  },
  {
   "text": "So let's start with policy, and it's pretty boring.",
   "start": 47,
   "end": 53.15
  },
  {
   "text": "I'm gonna go over here to my notes.",
   "start": 53.15,
   "end": 56.05
  },
  {
   "text": "So our starting point centers around policy, and.",
   "start": 56.05,
   "end": 61.55
  },
  {
   "text": "This sets the rules for how work gets done within the organization, and including especially risk compliance.",
   "start": 61.55,
   "end": 68.65
  },
  {
   "text": "Think of policy as the original institutional intent.",
   "start": 68.65,
   "end": 73.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Or the original system prompt.",
   "start": 73.85,
   "end": 76.8
  },
  {
   "text": "So ideally, we have this written down.",
   "start": 76.8,
   "end": 83.55
  },
  {
   "text": "It's a little bit boring, so stick with me.",
   "start": 76.8,
   "end": 83.55
  },
  {
   "text": "Using language like must, may, and should.",
   "start": 83.55,
   "end": 87.2
  },
  {
   "text": "And again, these help define the rules and decisions about how the system operates.",
   "start": 87.2,
   "end": 92.55
  },
  {
   "text": "In the organization, separate from policy, we have the actual running system.",
   "start": 92.55,
   "end": 99.75
  },
  {
   "text": "So the first thing we're going to do is separate these two.",
   "start": 99.75,
   "end": 107.15
  },
  {
   "text": "These two, both the build stage and the run stage, at two different moments in time.",
   "start": 107.15,
   "end": 111.7
  },
  {
   "text": "So typically, we're either defining or changing changing our policy.",
   "start": 111.7,
   "end": 115
  },
  {
   "text": "But the system is constantly running and it's constantly moving and changing.",
   "start": 115,
   "end": 121.5
  },
  {
   "text": "So we can then sort of imagine a compilation of a that.",
   "start": 121.5,
   "end": 128.35
  },
  {
   "text": "Oops! Sorry, let's skip ahead.",
   "start": 128.35,
   "end": 133.05
  },
  {
   "text": "It's constantly changing.",
   "start": 128.35,
   "end": 133.05
  },
  {
   "text": "So. It's evolving quickly with these product-driven changes.",
   "start": 133.05,
   "end": 142.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Everything is expected to still be roughly bound by policy, but.",
   "start": 136.05,
   "end": 142.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Ultimately, we separate this from the run state and the build state.",
   "start": 142.3,
   "end": 149.55
  },
  {
   "text": "The inside the system.",
   "start": 149.55,
   "end": 152.4
  },
  {
   "text": "What does it look like?",
   "start": 152.4,
   "end": 158.1
  },
  {
   "text": "We have a familiar model.",
   "start": 152.4,
   "end": 158.1
  },
  {
   "text": "If we have any enterprise folks in the room here.",
   "start": 152.4,
   "end": 158.1
  },
  {
   "text": "People processing technology, but we're really the agents.",
   "start": 158.1,
   "end": 165.2
  },
  {
   "text": "So I see them as an operational model cutting across all three.",
   "start": 165.2,
   "end": 172.05
  },
  {
   "text": "They work with people, execute parts of the process.",
   "start": 172.05,
   "end": 176.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Themselves, and they use and are made up of technology.",
   "start": 176.1,
   "end": 182.45
  },
  {
   "text": "So for our talk today, we're going to be focusing here where agents need process.",
   "start": 182.45,
   "end": 189.4
  },
  {
   "text": "What work we give them, what boundaries we set, and how we build trust in their outputs.",
   "start": 189.4,
   "end": 196.55
  },
  {
   "text": "So let's dive into your workflow.",
   "start": 199.7,
   "end": 204.15
  },
  {
   "text": "And it's high level when it seems basic.",
   "start": 204.15,
   "end": 207.95
  },
  {
   "text": "But if you haven't, there are good reasons to map this out.",
   "start": 207.95,
   "end": 213.5
  },
  {
   "text": "So maybe a change has to be approved before it goes live, or a customer goes through.",
   "start": 213.5,
   "end": 218.7
  },
  {
   "text": "Has to go through verification before their account is opened.",
   "start": 218.7,
   "end": 222.3
  },
  {
   "text": "We expect work to flow in a specific and gated direction.",
   "start": 222.3,
   "end": 229.5
  },
  {
   "text": "So I believe it makes.",
   "start": 229.5,
   "end": 232.35
  },
  {
   "text": "Agents make it worth revisiting what we do in parallel.",
   "start": 232.35,
   "end": 238.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Previously, some work used to cost too much or be too complex to coordinate in this way.",
   "start": 238.1,
   "end": 243.7
  },
  {
   "text": "Now we can run independent reviews alongside each other.",
   "start": 243.7,
   "end": 248.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Bring results together, but keep the required checks in place.",
   "start": 248.3,
   "end": 254.65
  },
  {
   "text": "So this is a directed acyclic graph, or a DAG.",
   "start": 254.65,
   "end": 258.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Is a way to represent this workflow or process: the steps, the dependencies.",
   "start": 258.9,
   "end": 264.4
  },
  {
   "text": "For a flow that moves forward without looking back on itself.",
   "start": 264.4,
   "end": 269.75
  },
  {
   "text": "Apache Airflow, if you're familiar, is an example of open source software that.",
   "start": 269.75,
   "end": 274.69
  }
 ],
